<p>Standard homeowners, commercial, and TWIA policies generally exclude flood; flood coverage usually comes from the National Flood Insurance Program or a private flood policy. Read <a href="/wind-vs-flood-damage-port-arthur-insurance/">wind vs. flood damage in Port Arthur</a> for how the two are separated.</p>

<h2>Fire and smoke damage</h2>
<p>Fire damage does not end when the flames are out. Smoke, soot, and heat can affect framing, wiring, HVAC systems, and contents in ways that are not obvious at first, and water used to fight the fire adds another layer of damage. Fire-related claims we work on include structural fire damage, smoke and soot contamination, water damage from firefighting, odor problems, and partial or total losses. See <a href="/services/fire-damage-claims/">fire damage claims</a> and <a href="/services/smoke-damage-claims/">smoke damage claims</a>.</p>

<h2>Additional covered losses</h2>
<p>Not every loss fits neatly into one category. We also review claims involving structural collapse, theft and vandalism, vehicle or tree impact, and damage to equipment and contents. If you are unsure whether a loss is covered, we can read your policy with you and explain your options before a costly mistake is made.</p>

