<p>Read more in <a href="/denied-insurance-claim-port-arthur/">what to do after a denied insurance claim in Port Arthur</a>.</p>

<h2>Reopening previously settled claims</h2>
<p>Many policyholders assume a closed claim is final. Often it is not. Depending on the policy and the timeline, a claim may be supplemented or reopened when:</p>
<ul>
<li>Additional damage surfaced later</li>
<li>Repairs uncovered hidden damage, such as wet insulation or mold behind walls</li>
<li>Pricing or scope in the original estimate was incomplete</li>
<li>The payment did not reflect real repair costs</li>
</ul>
<p>Our <a href="/services/insurance-claim-supplements/">insurance claim supplements</a> service addresses these situations. When the disagreement is over the amount of the loss rather than coverage, the policy's <a href="/services/insurance-appraisal/">insurance appraisal</a> clause may also be an option. Check your policy for deadlines, and consult a Texas attorney about any deadline to file suit.</p>

<h2>How our service process works</h2>
<p>Every claim is different, but our approach is consistent:</p>
